WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:05.980
sometimes when we talk about a political issue
on the show or a legal issue or a socio cultural

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:06.980
issue, two,

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.080
we talk and really specific technicalities.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.929
Everything is couched in a variety of details
and sort of nuanced and sophisticated ways

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:18.720
with caveats and ifs and ands and buts.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.029
And very often that's actually the right analysis
to do.

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:24.630
We want to be careful, we want to be thorough,
we want to be detailed.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.169
And the problem with it is that sometimes
I, as much as anybody else, we'll end up kind

00:00:29.169 --> 00:00:30.599
of getting lost in those details.

00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:37.120
And I will to apply a common, a proverb or,
or term or metaphor or analogy, I will miss

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.530
the forest for the trees.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:44.820
We forget that we're in a forest because we're
busy trying to count and measure every single

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.050
tree, for example.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:50.290
And Hillary Clinton actually did something
clever last night on the Rachel Maddow show.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:54.850
And this may come as a shock to many people
in our audience, but I'm not a Hillary fan

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.080
and I don't watch Rachel Maddow's show.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:58.860
I don't really watch MSNBC.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.740
The last time I talked about Rachel Maddow
was years ago when she bogusly hyped up having

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.260
Trump's tax returns.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:11.350
And what she had was like the first page of
Trump's oh five return, which had nothing

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:16.740
interesting in it other than showing that
most of the tax that Trump paid, uh, was as

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.790
a result of the alternative minimum tax.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.930
So people know Hillary's well to my right.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.270
I don't watch these shows or whatever.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.410
But this is actually a pretty interesting
clip.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:29.000
Hillary Clinton said last night on the Rachel
Maddow show.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.200
Hold on a second.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.479
Let's step back for a moment in terms of Trump
and Russia.

00:01:33.479 --> 00:01:42.390
And Mueller from was collusion or a obstruction
established, which evidence thresholds do

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:49.580
these different legal terms allude to exactly
how partisan was William bars handling of

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:50.740
this entire thing.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.140
Hillary Clinton steps back from the trees
and says, let's look at the forest for a second.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.799
And she lays out a really great hypothetical.

00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:03.530
Imagine if a Democrat went on live television,
uh, and said, China, if you're listening,

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.979
going get Trump's taxes.

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:11.989
And then hours later the IRS got hacked and
Trump's taxes were released and we found out

00:02:11.989 --> 00:02:17.890
that it was actually China who hacked and
provided those taxes to some third party,

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:20.230
like a Wiki leaks sort of organization.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.029
Hillary Clinton is stepping back from the
trees and remembering that we're in the forest.

00:02:24.029 --> 00:02:26.150
Take a look at what she said last night.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:30.099
Since Russia is clearly backing Republicans.

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:32.360
Why don't we ask China to back us?

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.519
I hear by tonight ask China.

00:02:34.519 --> 00:02:35.519
That's right.

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:40.639
And not only that, China, if you're listening,
why don't you get Trump's tax returns?

00:02:40.639 --> 00:02:44.719
I'm sure our media would richly reward you.

00:02:44.719 --> 00:02:51.180
Now, according to the Mueller report, that
is not conspiracy because it's done right

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:52.810
out in the open.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:59.470
So if after this hypothetical Democratic candidate
says this on your show, within hours, all

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:06.609
of a sudden the IRS offices are bombarded
with incredibly sophisticated cyber tools

00:03:06.609 --> 00:03:12.900
looking for Trump's tax returns and then extract
them and then passes them to whatever the

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:19.220
new wikileaks happens to be, and they start
being unraveled and disclosed.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.400
Nothing wrong with that.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:25.919
So the point of playing this is not to, uh,
uh, Praise Hillary.

00:03:25.919 --> 00:03:30.379
I mean, I thought that she was a bad candidate
and she's well to my right, the point of this

00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:35.060
is not to, to, to revisit the idea that Trump
